t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t203 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t204 Text What range does the p duration of this 12-lead ECG <TS>,...<TS> fallin? Answers:\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t205 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t206 Text 1.above the normalrange 2. below the normal range 3. within the normal range\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t207 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t208 Text Rationale\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t209 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t210 Text Clinical Context: 74-year-old\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t211 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t212 Text female patient. 12-lead ECG.\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t213 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t214 Text clinical recording. recorded with\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t215 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t216 Text AT-60 3. Signal quality: baseline\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t217 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t218 Text drift noted, static noise pre-sent,\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t219 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t220 Text burst noise present, electrode\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t221 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t222 Text artifacts present. extra beats\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t223 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t224 Text detected. pacemaker present.\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t225 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t226 Text To determine the P wave duration, we must first consider the standard normal\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t227 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t228 Text range, which is typically 0.08 to 0.11 seconds. In this ECG, despite the\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t229 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t230 Text presence of baseline drift, static noise, burst noise, and electrode artifacts,\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t231 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t232 Text the P waves can still be evaluated. The presence of a pacemaker may\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t233 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t234 Text influence the rhythm, but it does not directly affect the intrinsic P wave\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t235 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t236 Text duration. The P waves appear consistent across the leads, and even with the\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t237 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t238 Text noted artifacts, they do not seem prolonged. Given the patient's age and the\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t239 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t240 Text presence of a pacemaker, it is crucial to assess whether any conduction\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t241 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t242 Text abnormalities could affect the P wave duration. However, the morphology and\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t243 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t244 Text duration of the P waves do not suggest any significant prolongation.\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t245 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t246 Text Therefore, considering the observed patterns and clinical context, the P wave\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t247 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t248 Text duration falls within the normal range. Answer: within the normal range\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t249 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t250 Text OpenTSLM Paper\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t251 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t252 Text ICML\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t253 Text Intenational Con\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t254 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t255 Text OpenTSLM Github\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t256 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t257 Text Starred 1.2k\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t258 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t259 Text ETH zürich AGENTIC SYSTEMS LAB Collaborators: Stanford\r\nUniversity Google\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t260 Text Ende des extrahierten Textes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t261 container Seite 9\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t262 Text STEP-BY-STEP\r\nREASONING\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t263 Text During the first 5 minutes, RPM and electrical rise smoothly, but CHT shows \r\nirregular step-like oscillations with brief spikes (~0.15 units) and a slow upward \r\ndrift not correlated with power or mixture. EGT trends downward despite increasing \r\nRPM, and oil system signal decays with jitter. The combination points to unstable \r\ncooling airflow around a cylinder-consistent with a loose/damaged baffle tie/tie rod \r\ncausing baffle flutter and leakage.\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t264 Text Inspect engine cooling baffles, tie/tie-rod hardware, and seals around the affected \r\ncylinder(s). Tighten or replace the baffle tie/tie-rod, restore baffle seals, and secure \r\nall fasteners and brackets.\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t265 Text CHT will stabilize with a lower average and reduced variability (spikes eliminated, \r\n<+0.03 units), EGT will track power more normally (no persistent decline), and oil \r\nsystem readings will stabilize without jitter.\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t266 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t267 Text STATE SUMMARY\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t268 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t269 Text RECOMMENDED ACTION\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t270 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t271 Text EXPECTED OUTCOME\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t272 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t273 Text TIME-SERIES INPUT \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t274 Text Engine Temperature\r\nOil Parameters\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t275 Text Engine \r\nPerformance \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t276 Text Electrical \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t277 Text Fuel System\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t278 Text Engine\r\nConditio n (RPM)\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t279 Text 1. Analyze the sensor patterns to identify potential issues or anomalies\r\n2. Recommend specific maintenance actions to address the problems\r\n3. Predict the expected outcome if those maintenance actions are taken\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t280 Kopfzeile 2\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t281 Text PROMPT INPUT\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t282 Text GPT 5.5 · 1M context\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t283 Text CO NT EX T F ULL\r\nOpenTSLM ~25 min\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t284 Text At ~200K tokens / 5 min, a text window is spent in ~25 minutes. OpenTSLM \r\nstreams long, multivariate signal natively.\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t285 Text NO C ON TE XT WAL L\r\n\n\t\t\t\t\t