{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:02:27.268Z","ordinal":19255,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a09a00-35a0-7cd1-9c07-228bd416320f","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa6669ca95487d2a9e1ee6d0c380c0d","summary_text":["**Addressing integration issues**\n\nI need to mention to my friend that they should restart their machine if necessary, using the command `cd data_sourcing && uv run uvicorn ... --port 8001`. However, I might not need to go into that detail. It’s important to check if their service is running and the environment is loaded. There seems to be a mismatch between the expected port in documentation; the default command mentions port 8000 while we started on 8001, causing possible errors."],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1789290140716,"completed_at_ms":1789290147268}}
