{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:02:28.504Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa666a3235887d2b87f39331034f62e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a09a00-35a0-7cd1-9c07-228bd416320f"},"summary":[{"text":"**Addressing integration issues**\n\nI need to mention to my friend that they should restart their machine if necessary, using the command `cd data_sourcing \u0026\u0026 uv run uvicorn ... --port 8001`. However, I might not need to go into that detail. It’s important to check if their service is running and the environment is loaded. There seems to be a mismatch between the expected port in documentation; the default command mentions port 8000 while we started on 8001, causing possible errors.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:02:29.097Z","ordinal":19259,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09736-d5c6-7cc3-a099-0521c0b02bd2","turn_id":"01a09a00-35a0-7cd1-9c07-228bd416320f","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0f3535a43349ee3d016aa666a4676487d2866dd7ad012a8eb4","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"You’re right—we should include it. The actual issue is a startup mismatch: the frontend expects the sourcing service on **8001**, while its README/default launcher still says **8000**. I’m aligning that now so your friend’s Tavily `.env` works without a special command."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1789290148504,"completed_at_ms":1789290149097}}
